# Mastra-first (Syraa harness)

Mastra is the **agent app framework**. Use its primitives before writing our own runtime code.

## Default: use Mastra

When adding or changing agent behavior, check Mastra (and `@mastra/ai-sdk`, AI SDK UI) first:

| Need | Prefer |
|---|---|
| Chat loop | `agent.generate` / `agent.stream` |
| Streaming to UI | `toAISdkStream`, `handleChatStream`, `pipeUIMessageStreamToResponse`, `useChat` |
| Tools | `createTool` on the agent |
| Thread + history | Mastra Memory (`thread`, `resource`) — not client `history[]` as SoT |
| Working memory | Mastra thread WM — not DIY bootstrap/pin messages |
| Storage | Mastra storage on shared Postgres |
| Structured output | Mastra `structuredOutput` / AI SDK message stream — not hand-rolled SSE event protocols |

Docs: [mastra.ai/docs](https://mastra.ai/docs), `@mastra/ai-sdk` (`handleChatStream`, `toAISdkStream`).

## Keep ours (domain only)

These stay Syraa-owned and **must not import Mastra**:

- `@syraa/memory` — product prefs/rules/decisions (HITL)
- `@syraa/context` — materials, topics, chunks, retrieve
- `@syraa/ingest` — PDF ingest worker

Wire domain data **into** Mastra via tools, processors, or dynamic instructions — do not reimplement Mastra Memory or the agent loop.

## When custom code is OK

Write our own layer only when:

1. Mastra has no equivalent, or
2. The gap is explicit product logic (e.g. `applyLessons`, Works thread metadata, ingest upload), or
3. A Mastra primitive is blocked and the workaround is documented in code/plan.

If you add a custom stream protocol, event bus, or message parser, **stop** and check whether `@mastra/ai-sdk` + AI SDK UI already covers it.

## Review bar

PRs that add harness chat/stream/tool code should answer: *Why isn’t this `handleChatStream` / `createTool` / Memory / processors?*
